doc: PredProg: the filter's predicate is a program of literals (PredN: kop.FilterProgID, an index into Table.FilterProgs). The matcher applies the struct's own fields first (types, colours, controller, zone, flags, the Or chain), which are the program's first conjuncts, then evaluates each kop.FLit in order and stops at the first that fails; a literal's Neg inverts its word. Each word is a kop.FilterWord with one kernel handler (dirac/filter_<name>.go). A word reading a field its matcher does not have fails closed, as gorge's unbound context does. kgen lowers it for a clause whose comparisons the filter struct cannot hold (dirac/kgen/filter_spill.go); the words so far are the struct's own Pred codes re-expressed (power, toughness, mana value, counters, keyword, subtype).
